Partsmith's patch to OCCT 7.9.3 (tag V7_9_3, commit a016080bf6738d6aeae020badee4e888ad1540a5).

scripts/build-occt.sh applies it with git apply before the build, to its fresh clone of the tag
or to an unchanged clone of the pinned commit. scripts/occt-source-archive.sh adds it to the OCCT
source archive (delivery.md section 2.13, ADR 0073 in docs/adr/). It changes OCCT's code and is
offered under OCCT's own license, the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 with the
Open CASCADE exception. It is written so it can be offered to OCCT upstream.

It fixes a stack overflow and a null dereference that end the process while
STEPControl_Reader::ReadStream reads a STEP file (delivery.md section 3.8, findings 5 and 6):

1. RWStepShape_RWOrientedEdge::ReadStep. An ORIENTED_EDGE whose edge_element is an ORIENTED_EDGE
   breaks ISO 10303-42 oriented_edge WR1. StepShape_OrientedEdge::EdgeStart and EdgeEnd follow the
   edge_element, and a cycle of oriented edges, which OCCT's error recovery on a malformed file can
   build, makes them call each other until the stack overflows. The reader now gives the fail
   "edge_element is an oriented_edge" and drops the edge_element. EdgeStart and EdgeEnd then
   recurse at most one step. A reader that stops on a fail of the check list before the transfer,
   as Partsmith's does, never builds the shape.

2. RWStepShape_RWEdgeCurve::ReadStep. An EDGE_CURVE whose start or end is a plain VERTEX loaded
   without a fail. AreEndsMatch, in the check of the edge curve, then read the point of a null
   VertexPoint, and StepToTopoDS_TranslateVertex::Init reads the same null point in the transfer.
   The reader now asks for a VertexPoint at both ends, and any other vertex gives the load fail
   "Parameter n0.2 (edge_start) : Entity has illegal type" or the same for edge_end. The check
   then skips the edge curve, which failed to load.

diff --git a/src/RWStepShape/RWStepShape_RWEdgeCurve.cxx b/src/RWStepShape/RWStepShape_RWEdgeCurve.cxx
index 408de879..c36353dc 100644
--- a/src/RWStepShape/RWStepShape_RWEdgeCurve.cxx
+++ b/src/RWStepShape/RWStepShape_RWEdgeCurve.cxx
@@ -127,12 +127,13 @@ void RWStepShape_RWEdgeCurve::ReadStep(const Handle(StepData_StepReaderData)& th
   theStepData->ReadString(theRecordID, 1, "name", theMessageTool, aName);
 
   // --- inherited field : edgeStart ---
+  // Both vertices must be VertexPoints: the check and the transfer read their points
   Handle(StepShape_Vertex) anEdgeStart;
   theStepData->ReadEntity(theRecordID,
                           2,
                           "edge_start",
                           theMessageTool,
-                          STANDARD_TYPE(StepShape_Vertex),
+                          STANDARD_TYPE(StepShape_VertexPoint),
                           anEdgeStart);
 
   // --- inherited field : edgeEnd ---
@@ -141,7 +142,7 @@ void RWStepShape_RWEdgeCurve::ReadStep(const Handle(StepData_StepReaderData)& th
                           3,
                           "edge_end",
                           theMessageTool,
-                          STANDARD_TYPE(StepShape_Vertex),
+                          STANDARD_TYPE(StepShape_VertexPoint),
                           anEdgeEnd);
 
   // --- own field : edgeGeometry ---
diff --git a/src/RWStepShape/RWStepShape_RWOrientedEdge.cxx b/src/RWStepShape/RWStepShape_RWOrientedEdge.cxx
index c8948573..03bc0c8a 100644
--- a/src/RWStepShape/RWStepShape_RWOrientedEdge.cxx
+++ b/src/RWStepShape/RWStepShape_RWOrientedEdge.cxx
@@ -52,6 +52,13 @@ void RWStepShape_RWOrientedEdge::ReadStep(const Handle(StepData_StepReaderData)&
   Handle(StepShape_Edge) aEdgeElement;
   // szv#4:S4163:12Mar99 `Standard_Boolean stat4 =` not needed
   data->ReadEntity(num, 4, "edge_element", ach, STANDARD_TYPE(StepShape_Edge), aEdgeElement);
+  // The edge_element must not be an oriented_edge (ISO 10303-42 oriented_edge WR1): EdgeStart and
+  // EdgeEnd follow it, and a cycle of oriented edges makes them recurse without end
+  if (!aEdgeElement.IsNull() && aEdgeElement->IsKind(STANDARD_TYPE(StepShape_OrientedEdge)))
+  {
+    ach->AddFail("edge_element is an oriented_edge");
+    aEdgeElement.Nullify();
+  }
 
   // --- own field : orientation ---
 
